d columns into rectangular compartments, infer the separator, background, and marker colors from the grid and demonstrations. Output one cell per compartment, preserving compartment order. In the demonstrated family, use color 1 when a compartment contains at least two occurrences of the marker color; otherwise use the original background color. Count markers anywhere inside each compartment, excluding separator lines. Derive output dimensions from the number of compartments, not the number of separator lines. Verify the threshold, colors, boundaries, and output dimensions against every available demonstration before applying the rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:42:44.443Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:42:44.443Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682188/attempts/097eda31949a4b61b5f7193c1d3e6907/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929134319108","summary":"Added a global memory for separator-compartment marker counting, with a caution against treating the observed threshold as universal.","rationale":"The solved test and the second demo support marking compartments containing at least two markers, but the first demo includes an apparent one-marker exception, so the rule needs a clear uncertainty caveat.","expectedOutcome":"Future solutions can recognize compartment-compression tasks, infer marker thresholds from all demonstrations, and avoid overgeneralizing when an example conflicts with a simple count rule.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_separator_compartment_marker_count_threshold_with_demo_validation","title":"ARC separator compartments: infer marker-count rule from demonstrations","content":"For ARC grids partitioned into rectangular compartments by full separator rows and/or columns, produce one output cell per compartment when demonstrations support compression. Identify separator, background, and marker colors from the grid and demos; count markers separately within each compartment. A threshold of at least two markers mapping to color 1, with fewer mapping to the background color, matched one demonstrated task's second demo and solved test. Do not assume this threshold universally: another demo in that task family appeared to map a one-marker compartment to 1. Check every compartment in every demonstration, including apparent exceptions, and infer any additional shape, color, or positional condition before applying the rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Stores the reusable solved-task pattern while explicitly recording conflicting demonstration evidence to discourage unsupported generalization.","after":{"id":"arc_separator_compartment_marker_count_threshold_with_demo_validation","kind":"memory","title":"ARC separator compartments: infer marker-count rule from demonstrations","content":"For ARC grids partitioned into rectan