{"id":"refine_20260929134350350","summary":"Updated the separator-compartment memory with the demonstrated color-count threshold and output rule.","rationale":"The solved example validates a specific rule for separator-divided compartments, and an existing global memory already covers inferring marker-count rules; updating it avoids duplicating that guidance.","expectedOutcome":"For similar ARC grids, infer compartment boundaries and the marker threshold from demonstrations, then validate each compressed output cell against the rule.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_separator_compartment_marker_count_threshold_with_demo_validation","title":"ARC separator compartments: infer marker-count rule from demonstrations","content":"For ARC grids partitioned by full-color separator rows and/or columns into rectangular compartments, demonstrations may support compressing each compartment to one output cell. Infer the separator, compartment dimensions, sparse marker color, threshold, output marker color, and default/background color from the examples; do not treat any threshold as universal. Validated example: a 19×19 grid divided by full color-6 rows and columns forms 5×4 compartments, each 3×4 cells. The output is 5×4: use color 1 when a compartment contains at least two color-3 cells, otherwise color 2. Derive compartment boundaries from the separators and check every output cell's marker count against the inferred rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a successful, concrete demonstration to the existing general memory while preserving its caution to infer task-specific rules.","before":{"id":"arc_separator_compartment_marker_count_threshold_with_demo_validation","kind":"memory","title":"ARC separator compartments: infer marker-count rule from demonstrations","content":"For ARC grids partitioned into rectangular compartments by full separator rows and/or columns, produce one output cell per compartment when demonstrations support co