{"id":"refine_20260929134921936","summary":"Added a global ARC memory for decoding compartment colors from four-corner separator markers.","rationale":"The solved task and demonstrations support checking all four marker values at each compartment’s corners: emit the shared non-background color only when all four agree, otherwise emit the compartment fill color. The active separator range must be inferred rather than assumed from the full grid dimensions.","expectedOutcome":"On similar tiled ARC grids, infer the active separator intervals and construct the corresponding output cell by cell; validate dimensions and each four-corner comparison against demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_separator_compartment_four_corner_marker_agreement","title":"ARC separator compartments: emit colors when all four corners agree","content":"For ARC grids tiled into uniform-background compartments by horizontal and vertical separator lines, marker values at separator intersections may encode each compartment. Infer the active consecutive separator rows and columns from the grid and demonstrations; do not assume the entire grid is active. For each compartment interval, inspect the four marker values at its corner intersections. Output the shared marker color if all four corners have the same non-background value; otherwise output the compartment fill/background color. Output dimensions equal the number of active row intervals by column intervals. Validate the interval selection and each corner comparison against demonstrations. Validated example: active row coordinates 0, 3, 6, 9, 12 and column coordinates 0, 4, 8, 12 yield [[4,7,2],[7,7,7],[8,7,1],[7,7,1]].","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The solved task and multiple demonstrations support this reusable corner-agreement decoding rule.","after":{"id":"arc_separator_compartment_four_corner_marker_agreement","kind":"memory","title":"ARC separator compartments: emit colors when all four corners agree","content":"For ARC grids tiled into uniform-background compartments by horizontal and vertical separator lines, marker values at separator intersections may encode each compartment. Infer the active consecutive separator rows and columns from the grid and demonstrations; do not assume the entire grid is active. For each compartment interval, inspect the four marker values at its corner intersections. Output the shared marker color if all four corners have the same non-background value; otherwise output the compartment fill/background color. Output dimensions equal the number of active row intervals by column intervals. Validate the interval selection and each corner comparison against demonstrations. Validated example: active row coordinates 0, 3, 6, 9, 12 and column coordinates 0, 4, 8, 12 yield [[4,7,2],[7,7,7],[8,7,1],[7,7,1]].","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:49:31.380Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:49:31.380Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682188/attempts/097eda31949a4b61b5f7193c1d3e6907/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929135721328","summary":"Updated the global ARC compartment-replication memory with a validated example and a caution against unsupported copying.","rationale":"Task-4b86ffd4 confirms that a pattern in one compartment was copied to corresponding blank compartments, while the existing memory already covers this general task family.","expectedOutcome":"Future solutions can recognize demonstrated compartment-pattern propagation, preserve separators and dimensions, and validate that copying is supported by the demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_separator_compartments_replicate_occupied_motif","title":"ARC separator compartments: replicate a demonstrated occupied motif","content":"For ARC grids partitioned by full separator rows and/or columns into equal-sized compartments, demonstrations may show an occupied compartment's entire local pattern being copied into corresponding blank compartments. Preserve each compartment's dimensions, all copied cell values (including background), separator lines, and overall grid dimensions. Validate the source compartment, destination compartments, and any position alignment against the demonstrations; do not copy when compartments contain distinct content or the rule is unsupported. Validated task-4b86ffd4: a 17x7 grid with 0 separators had three 5x3 panels; a marker in one panel was copied to the same local position in the other panels. The 5x11 test had 7-colored separator columns at indices 3 and 7; the left 3x3 pattern was copied into both other panels, and the submission was correct.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The solved instance provides cross-session evidence for the existing compartment-replication memory and specifies alignment and applicability safeguards.","before":{"id":"arc_separator_compartments_replicate_occupied_motif","kind":"memory","title":"ARC separator compartments replicate occupied motif","content":"Task family: separator-grid tiling/replication. Full horizontal and vertical separator lines partition a grid into equal rectangular compartments. One compartment contains a motif and the others are blank background; output repeats the whole motif, cell by cell, into every compartment while preserving separator lines and motif values. Validated task-4b86ffd4: 11x14 grid separated by color 3 at row 5 and columns 4,9, making 5x4 compartments in a 2x3 layout. The occupied bottom-right tile (rows 6-10, columns 10-13) was [[6,0,9,9],[6,1,5,5],[5,5,5,5],[5,1,0,9],[5,5,6,5]]. The correct output copied this tile identically into all six compartments and retained separators. Demo confirms the same rule: 11x13 grid split by row 5 and column 6; its top-left 5x6 tile was replicated into the other three compartments. For similar tasks, locate the non-background tile, infer equal compartment dimensions, and repeat its pattern across all compartments. The output retains full grid dimensions; do not confuse this with compartment-marker compression.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:57:05.516315+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:57:05.516333+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_separator_compartments_replicate_occupied_motif","kind":"memory","title":"ARC separator compartments: replicate a demonstrated occupied motif","content":"For ARC grids partitioned by full separator rows and/or columns into equal-sized compartments, demonstrations may show an occupied compartment's entire local pattern being copied into corresponding blank compartments. Preserve each compartment's dimensions, all copied cell values (including background), separator lines, and overall grid dimensions. Validate the source compartment, destination compartments, and any position alignment against the demonstrations; do not copy when compartments contain distinct content or the rule is unsupported. Validated task-4b86ffd4: a 17x7 grid with 0 separators had three 5x3 panels; a marker in one panel was copied to the same local position in the other panels. The 5x11 test had 7-colored separator columns at indices 3 and 7; the left 3x3 pattern was copied into both other panels, and the submission was correct.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:57:05.516315+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:57:27.940Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682188/attempts/097eda31949a4b61b5f7193c1d3e6907/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929135921253","summary":"Created a global memory capturing the demonstrated compartment-copying pattern and its unresolved failed test case.","rationale":"Multiple demonstrations support copying a seed motif into blank compartments at identical local offsets, but every attempted application to the 9×9 test was incorrect, so the rule needs a clear uncertainty warning.","expectedOutcome":"Future solutions can recognize demonstrated same-orientation compartment repetition while avoiding confident extrapolation to the unresolved cross-shaped case; validate candidate rules against all examples and seek discriminating evidence.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_compartment_motif_copy_task_4b86ffd4_unresolved_test","title":"ARC compartment motif copying: demonstrated repetition with unresolved cross case","content":"In ARC grids with a uniform background and full separator rows/columns dividing compartments, demonstrations in task-4b86ffd4 showed a nonempty seed compartment copied unchanged into corresponding blank compartments at the same local row/column offsets. Demos 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, and 8 support repetition, including across both axes where applicable; do not assume reflection when exact same orientation is demonstrated. Demo 5 also showed stripe/repeated-color pattern effects, so inspect each task's examples rather than forcing a single rule. Important unresolved counterevidence: on the 9×9 test with background 7, separator 9, and a central cross dividing four 4×4 regions, the upper-right seed had local cells (1,0)=1, (2,1)=1, (3,1)=3, (3,2)=1. Attempts copying unchanged to all other compartments, copying vertically only, and reflected variants all failed. The correct transformation or trigger remains unknown; do not confidently apply basic compartment copying to a similar case without further evidence. Validate candidate rules against every demo and treat this failed test as a warning, not as evidence for any particular alternative.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC"},"reason":"Preserves a repeated demonstrated rule alongside a concrete failed generalization, helping future solutions recognize the pattern without repeating unsupported guesses.","after":{"id":"arc_compartment_motif_copy_task_4b86ffd4_unresolved_test","kind":"memory","title":"ARC compartment motif copying: demonstrated repetition with unresolved cross case","content":"In ARC grids with a uniform background and full separator rows/columns dividing compartments, demonstrations in task-4b86ffd4 showed a nonempty seed compartment copied unchanged into corresponding blank compartments at the same local row/column offsets. Demos 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, and 8 support repetition, including across both axes where applicable; do not assume reflection when exact same orientation is demonstrated. Demo 5 also showed stripe/repeated-color pattern effects, so inspect each task's examples rather than forcing a single rule. Important unresolved counterevidence: on the 9×9 test with background 7, separator 9, and a central cross dividing four 4×4 regions, the upper-right seed had local cells (1,0)=1, (2,1)=1, (3,1)=3, (3,2)=1. Attempts copying unchanged to all other compartments, copying vertically only, and reflected variants all failed. The correct transformation or trigger remains unknown; do not confidently apply basic compartment copying to a similar case without further evidence. Validate candidate rules against every demo and treat this failed test as a warning, not as evidence for any particular alternative.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:59:28.291Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:59:28.291Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682188/attempts/097eda31949a4b61b5f7193c1d3e6907/system/sta