{"id":"refine_20260929140156809","summary":"Updated the global task-4b86ffd4 compartment-replication memory with the validated copying rule and an indexing safeguard.","rationale":"The task was solved after demonstrations confirmed same-local-coordinate motif copying across separator-defined compartments; earlier incorrect submissions came from misreading the middle compartment’s row contents.","expectedOutcome":"On similar compartment-replication tasks, copy supported motif cells without altering separators or dimensions, and verify compartment slices cell by cell before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_compartment_motif_replication_validated_task_4b86ffd4","title":"ARC compartment motif replication validated task-4b86ffd4","content":"Validated ARC task family: full separator rows and/or columns of a distinct color partition a uniform-background grid into rectangular compartments. Demonstrations show non-background motif cells copied between corresponding compartments at identical local coordinates, while preserving separator lines, dimensions, and all existing motif cells. Apply propagation only as supported by the demonstrations; copies may extend to adjacent compartments and layouts may be horizontal, vertical, or 2×2. In the solved 5×26 instance, separators at columns 8 and 17 bounded three 5×8 compartments; copy the occupied middle compartment’s motif into the left and right compartments. Index compartments and rows carefully: the middle compartment’s local row 1 was [7,5,7,7,7,2,1,1]. Earlier attempts misread it as [7,5,7,7,2,1,1,1], producing incorrect outputs. Before submission, compare every compartment’s exact local cells and confirm separators and dimensions are unchanged.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Validated by task-4b86ffd4 demonstrations and correct test submission."},"reason":"Preserves the successful general rule and a specific, demonstrated indexing failure that caused repeated incorrect submi