ation slice cell by cell; do not omit background cells or copy into only one band.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a confirmed two-axis repetition example and a concrete validation safeguard based on errors and eventual success in the task trajectory.","before":{"id":"arc_compartment_motif_replication_validated_task_4b86ffd4","kind":"memory","title":"ARC compartment motif replication validated task-4b86ffd4","content":"Validated ARC task family: full separator rows and/or columns of a distinct color partition a uniform-background grid into rectangular compartments. Demonstrations show non-background motif cells copied between corresponding compartments at identical local coordinates, while preserving separator lines, dimensions, and all existing motif cells. Apply propagation only as supported by the demonstrations; copies may extend to adjacent compartments and layouts may be horizontal, vertical, or 2×2. In the solved 5×26 instance, separators at columns 8 and 17 bounded three 5×8 compartments; copy the occupied middle compartment’s motif into the left and right compartments. Index compartments and rows carefully: the middle compartment’s local row 1 was [7,5,7,7,7,2,1,1]. Earlier attempts misread it as [7,5,7,7,2,1,1,1], producing incorrect outputs. Before submission, compare every compartment’s exact local cells and confirm separators and dimensions are unchanged.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Validated by task-4b86ffd4 demonstrations and correct test submission."},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:00:13.661993+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:03.542Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"arc_compartment_motif_replication_validated_task_4b86ffd4","kind":"memory","title":"ARC compartment motif replication validated task-4b86ffd4","content":"Validated ARC task family: uniform-background grids divided by full separator rows and/or columns into equal compartments. When demo