{"id":"refine_20260929144338482","summary":"Create a global memory preserving task-b321b148’s mixed ray-and-pattern evidence while explicitly recording that its rule remains unresolved.","rationale":"The demonstrations show isolated pixels becoming 4 with same-row rays in some cases, while other edge motifs produce periodic fills; the test instance was not solved despite eight attempts, so none of the attempted test rules should be treated as validated.","expectedOutcome":"Future encounters can use the observations as cautious clues, seek discriminating demonstrations, and avoid confidently repeating the failed extrapolations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_b321b148_mixed_edge_rays_unresolved","title":"ARC task-b321b148: mixed edge rays and fills, rule unresolved","content":"Evidence from task-b321b148 demonstrations is mixed; do not treat this as a fully inferred rule. In demo 6, isolated color-1 pixels on rows 9 and 10 become color 4, and color 1 fills along those rows from each pixel toward a matching color-6 strip at the right edge. In demo 7, isolated color-0 pixels become 4 and color 0 is drawn along their rows toward/from the left edge; the edge-strip relation is not a simple universal ray rule. Other demonstrations show edge motifs producing periodic or patterned fills, so do not assume every edge strip merely points at isolated pixels. The test instance (background 6, color-1 strips on the right in rows 0–1 and left in rows 2–3, isolated color 7 at row 2 column 2) remained unsolved after eight attempts. Attempts including a simple left-edge ray through column 1 to the isolated 7 (recoloring the dot to 4), and filling edge rows, were incorrect. Preserve this instance as unresolved; use additional demonstrations to distinguish candidate rules, and do not present those failed test proposals as validated.","metadata":{"scope":"global","task_id":"task-b321b148","status":"unresolved"},"reason":"Record the requested cross-sessio