{"id":"refine_20260929145752791","summary":"Added a global memory for task-1fccd3cf’s validated mirror-and-stack transformation.","rationale":"The trajectory records a correct test submission using the rule and provides demonstrations that support the 3H-by-2W output shape; the uniform-grid demo confirms the shape but does not distinguish band ordering.","expectedOutcome":"On recurring instances of task-1fccd3cf, construct each row as its horizontal reverse followed by the original row, then stack vertically reversed, original-order, and vertically reversed input bands; verify dimensions and band order before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_1fccd3cf_mirror_rows_three_bands","title":"task-1fccd3cf: mirror rows and stack three vertical bands","content":"Validated ARC task family task-1fccd3cf. For an H×W input, make each output row by concatenating the input row in reverse order with the original row, giving width 2W. Stack three bands vertically: the input rows in reverse order, then the input rows in original order, then the input rows in reverse order. Output dimensions are 3H×2W. Do not repeat each transformed row three times. The correct 8×4 test submission used this rule and produced a 24×8 output. Demonstrations include a 1×4 input with a 3×8 output (which confirms horizontal mirroring and height expansion but cannot distinguish vertical band order), a 9×11 input with a 27×22 output, and a uniform 3×7 input with a uniform 9×14 output (which corroborates dimensions but does not distinguish ordering).","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-1fccd3cf"},"reason":"The transformation was validated by a correct test submission and is useful if this task recurs with a fresh input.","after":{"id":"arc_task_1fccd3cf_mirror_rows_three_bands","kind":"memory","title":"task-1fccd3cf: mirror rows and stack three vertical bands","content":"Validated ARC task family task-1fccd3cf. For an H×W input, make each output row by concatenating the input row in reverse order with the original row, giving width 2W. Stack three bands vertically: the input rows in reverse order, then the input rows in original order, then the input rows in reverse order. Output dimensions are 3H×2W. Do not repeat each transformed row three times. The correct 8×4 test submission used this rule and produced a 24×8 output. Demonstrations include a 1×4 input with a 3×8 output (which confirms horizontal mirroring and height expansion but cannot distinguish vertical band order), a 9×11 input with a 27×22 output, and a uniform 3×7 input with a uniform 9×14 output (which corroborates dimensions but does not distinguish ordering).","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-1fccd3cf"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:58:01.722Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:58:01.722Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682188/attempts/097eda31949a4b61b5f7193c1d3e6907/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
